      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;checking-if-a-table-exists-in-sql-server&#34;&gt;Checking if a Table Exists in SQL Server&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When dealing with SQL Server databases, it&amp;rsquo;s essential to know how to check if a table exists. This article explores various methods, including using the INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES view, the OBJECT_ID() function, and alternative approaches.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;method-1-using-the-information_schematables-view&#34;&gt;Method 1: Using the INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES View&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES view provides a standard and database-independent way to check for table existence. The following SQL query demonstrates this method:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-sql&#34; data-lang=&#34;sql&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;IF&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;EXISTS&lt;/span&gt; (&lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;SELECT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;*&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;FROM&lt;/span&gt; INFORMATION_SCHEMA.TABLES &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;WHERE&lt;/span&gt; TABLE_TYPE&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;BASE TABLE&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;AND&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;TABLE_NAME&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;mytablename&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;) &#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;   &lt;span style=&#34;color:#66d9ef&#34;&gt;SELECT&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style=&#34;color